<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 54,265 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 54,265 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 54,265 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday, compared to 40,631 tonnes on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Tuesday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			26,446	    16,894</p>
<p>    Import cargo			27,819	    23,737</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships were expected to sail and eleven were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>General Cargo	  8,500	  Khairpur	     due</p>
<p>Crude oil		71,000	 Stavros-1	    due</p>
<p>High speed diesel    56,000	 Keefan		 7/2</p>
<p>Palm oil		 12,000	 Wawasan Courage    5/2</p>
<p>Furnace Oil	    40,000	 Trade Resolve	5/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
